verses.text:
Christians promoted to office, 511; persecution of, 496, 497;
cf. persecution, 512–13; kindly received by barbarians, 513; in Persia, 542;
not to be held slaves by Jews, 547; hypocritical Christians, 554.

Diocletian, persecution by, 485, 486; passes through
Palestine, 487; abdication of, 487, 579; insanity and cruelty of, 512;
terrified by lightning, 579.

Sons of C, 505, 582; heirs of Helena, 530, 531; appointed Cæsars,
550; empire divided between, 553; instruction of, 553, 554; Christians, 553;
proclaimed Augustus by the army, 557.
